WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.320
Absolutely!
I think anything else would be...

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.240
...strange and untrue. Of course it has.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:19.240
So can you trust people?
There are so many people around you-

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.240
-there's a lot of attention and praise,
but can you trust them?

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.200
Well, I have...
I find it quite hard to trust people.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:35.480
But that isn't because people...
It's not because I'm famous.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.680
It was harder when I was younger
and unknown. That's just in me.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.520
So in my life, it's more...

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.920
I'm happily and beautifully surprised
when I find that people are loyal-

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.120
-when they mean what they say,
stand by things, and show courage.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:02.280
So you don't always know where you are,
but you have a house in London.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:09.240
-Is that home for you?
-It has become my home, amazingly.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:15.160
I live there, and I have family
that lives there with me.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:20.800
I've actually started to find a team
that travels with me-

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.800
-that goes with me to movie sets
and works with me.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.680
-Has your son moved there too?
-Yes.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:33.240
-So... You've become a Brit?
-I've become a Brit, yes.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.920
-Nice.
-The most unlikely Brit...

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:42.160
When you gained
international recognition-

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.640
-from playing Lisbeth Salander,
you were...

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:53.640
It happened very suddenly, and as far
as I know, your English wasn't good.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:58.880
-Definitely not.
-Today you're on American talk shows...

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.040
...sounding like a perfect American.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:07.680
You speak it much better than I do.
How did you learn so quickly?

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.880
Okay, I actually learned how
in Oslo mostly.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.640
Okay...

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:22.240
I did a film called "Babycall"
that was shot in Oslo.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.480
I think I spent three months
living in Grand Hotel Oslo.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:32.760
I had done press conferences and
interviews for the Millennium Trilogy.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:39.520
It was horrendous. I panicked over not
being able to communicate or understand.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:46.160
I just felt so stupid,
unintelligent, and inferior.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:51.760
It made me just want to be nice
and well-liked. It was so primitive.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:57.400
I decided I didn't want that,
I had to make the language mine.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:02.160
I was in Oslo shooting the film,
and my character was complicated-

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.080
-so I didn't socialize at all.
I would spend my nights-

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:12.280
-watching BBC, CNN,
and movies without the subtitles.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:18.360
I would read anything from newspapers,
magazines, scripts.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.720
It took me an entire night
to read a script back then.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:27.280
Didn't you have a foundation
to stand on, from school?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:33.320
I hate being bad at things, and I had
to prioritize when I was younger.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:40.440
So English, languages, books,
reading, grammar, and so on...

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:44.480
I didn't make them a priority,
I learned other things.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.800
And you have...

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:52.720
You speak English, Swedish,
and some Icelandic?

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:57.240
-And you partly grew up there?
-Yes, my stepfather is Icelandic.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:03.720
-But your father is Spanish.
-Right. That's next on my to-do list.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:09.080
-Tell me, your father isn't alive?
-No.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:14.240
-Did you know him?
-We met, but I didn't know him.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.960
-How did you get in touch?
-We met when I was 15.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:23.520
My mom and he had mutual friends.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:28.880
I met him once then, again at around 19,
and then at 20.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.760
Then there was a gap,
a period when we didn't meet.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:39.680
I reached out to him again
after I became a mother.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:45.480
By then, he was ill from cancer.
We met a few times before he died.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:49.440
What kind of relationship
did you have with him?

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:58.000
We reached a point when I felt...

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:05.120
...that I wasn't angry anymore.
I understood his version, his struggles.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.760
It used to be very one-dimensional
on my part.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:12.440
But I ended up being reconciled.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:18.360
It was funny, I was holding his hand,
and I have pretty manly hands.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:25.000
I held his hand, and saw that our hands
were identical. It made me feel...

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:29.160
...a sense of calm.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:35.120
I felt this anger and harshness
just simmer down.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:41.680
-And it hasn't come back since.
-Are there other similarities?

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:47.800
I look a lot like him,
with the cheekbones and all of this.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:53.080
-Do you have a clear grasp of it all?
-No.

